TTYCHATTER.PYTHON(1)       User Commands       TTYCHATTER.PYTHON(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.python - Bash OpenRouter chat client with Python 3 helpers

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.python [session]
    ttychatter.python --demo [session]
    ttychatter.python --models
    ttychatter.python --routers
    ttychatter.python --test-model MODEL
    ttychatter.python --set-api-key
    ttychatter.python --forget-api-key
    ttychatter.python --doctor
    ttychatter.python --version
    ttychatter.python --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.python is the practical line-oriented Bash client. It uses Bash
    for orchestration, curl for OpenRouter HTTPS calls, and Python 3 helper
    snippets for JSON, URL escaping, path expansion, and safer parsing.

RUNTIME COMMANDS
    During interactive chat, colon commands are local ttychatter commands and
    are not sent to the AI model:

        :help
        :models
        :routers
        :select-model
        :test-model MODEL
        :favorites
        :favorite MODEL
        :unfavorite MODEL
        :config
        :set KEY VALUE
        :unset KEY
        :set-api-key
        :forget-api-key
        :memory
        :attach FILE
        :editor
        :credits
        :doctor
        :quit

API KEY STORAGE
    --set-api-key now presents storage choices:

        1) runtime only
        2) encrypted with gpg
        3) plaintext config

    If gpg is not installed, the command prints "gpg not found" and keeps the
    key runtime-only when encrypted storage is requested.

    Plaintext storage is still supported, but only after an explicit warning.

CONFIGURATION
    Default config file:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config

    Relevant keys:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
        THEME
        SEND_INPUT
        MODEL
        MODEL_TYPE_FILTER
        MODEL_SORT_ORDER
        CONTEXT_TURNS
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES

VERSION
    ttychatter.python version 3.10
